 + X("unknown payment", "a gateway that dies")),
("The restaurant refuses the order after the customer has already paid.",
 "functional", 5,
 "A separate path from a cancellation, because a different person is refusing and the money has already moved. "
 "REJECTED is a legal successor of PLACED and of nothing else, so a restaurant can only refuse an order it has not "
 "accepted yet. The method moves the state through the same guarded transition, gives the food back to the shelf, takes the "
 "order off the tablet's queue, refunds the whole bill &mdash; there is no fee, the customer did nothing wrong "
 "&mdash; and hands back any rider. Afterwards REJECTED is terminal, so a second tap on the restaurant's tablet "
 "throws instead of refunding twice, which is the part worth pointing at.",
 sect(src, "Refund reject(String orderId)", "Refund cancel(String orderId)")),
("The app asks 'where is my order?' a thousand times a second. Make it O(1), with no lock.",
